# Supabase Data API grants on new tables

From **2026-10-30**, Supabase no longer auto-grants Data API access to new tables in `public`.

When a migration `CREATE TABLE`s in `public`, add in the **same** migration:

```sql
grant select on public.your_table to anon;
grant select, insert, update, delete on public.your_table to authenticated;
grant select, insert, update, delete on public.your_table to service_role;
```

- Existing tables (already in prod) keep their grants — no backfill needed for them.
- `ALTER TABLE` alone does not need new grants.
- Fresh environments count as new tables: `supabase db reset`, preview branches, new projects.
